Note the `\n\` continuation with leading space on the next line — in Rust string continuation `\` at end of line strips the newline AND leading whitespace of next line. So `"\n\n\ 1."` equals `"\n\n1."`? Hmm wait — `"Focus on critical issues ONLY:\n\n\` then newline then ` 1. **Bugs**..."` — the `\` line continuation eats the newline and all leading whitespace on the next line. So the actual string is `"...ONLY:\n\n1. **Bugs**..."`. Wait no — look:

