 Skip style, performance, and minor suggestions. Be terse — one line per finding."
```

`\n\n\` — escape newline? No: `\n` is newline escape, then `\` at line end is continuation. So `"\n\n"` followed by continuation → next line's leading whitespace stripped → `1. **Bugs**...`. Then `\n\` → newline char + continuation → next line `2. **Security**...`. Then `\n\n\` → `\n\n` + continuation → `Skip style...`.

